==Russian==

===Etymology===
Borrowed in the second half of 18th century (first attested in 1785, form {{m|ru|барказ}} in 1762) from {{bor|ru|nl|barkas|t=a large or the largest row-boat on a ship}} (att. since 1718), {{bor|ru|sv|barkasse}} (since 1765) or possibly another Western European language, from some {{der|ru|roa|-}} language. Compare {{der|ru|it|barcaccia}}. Ultimately from {{der|ru|la|barca}}. {{doublet|ru|баржа́|ба́рка}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|барка́с}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Cinemantique-баркас.wav}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|барка́с}}

# [[launch]] ''(a big rowing boat)''
# [[longboat]]

